# Macro for plotting data sets at BL29 - operates with gnuplot 1.4
# HU & AB, June 1777

# user should enter a bunch of information at the top of the file, then the q positions in the middle
# the main working routine is 'gpi.63_analyzer_load' - this file must be located in the default directory
# the main plot routine is run by the command 'load make_page' - generally done several times for different ranges, scaling, etc
# note: there is the possibility to make cascade plots and log plots
# single quotes ' are usually used to delimit strings, contents of double quotes are evaluated first

# some explanation of parameters:
#    problem_name7 = main name for this data set and alsot he output files
#    resolution_name  = resolution file name - in principle this is measured with same slit setting and also processed with same bin size.
#    nmorefiles = how many more files other than the first one
#  for each plot (n = 0, nmorefiles+6)
#    ysfn = scale factor for rates - usually a6.  Can also be set for each file
#    tfn  = title string for file 9 - e.g. temperature
#    CLn  = color of line 

